---
source: crates/ym-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"info\"])"
---
Print metadata and the automatic estimates without rendering

Usage: ym info [OPTIONS] <FILES>...

Arguments:
  <FILES>...  ARW files to inspect

Options:
      --json                            Print one JSON object per file instead of text (the shape of `render --json` without `output` and `timings_ms`)
  -q, --quiet                           Print only errors on stderr
      --profile <ID>                    Force a camera profile, for comparisons (for example `sony-ilce-7rm4`)
  -v, --verbose                         Print what is happening on stderr: stages, timings and notes
      --apple-auto <on|off>             Apple Auto for this run. On a Mac with Apple Intelligence, Apple's on-device model grades each photo: it sets the automatic exposure, highlights, shadows, black, contrast, warmth, tint and saturation and the colours of the shadows and highlights. Default: the app's setting where Apple Auto is available, off elsewhere
      --apple-auto-instructions <FILE>  A text file with instructions for Apple's model, used for this run instead of those in Preferences (at most 2000 characters; an empty file is the default instructions)
  -h, --help                            Print help
